================================================================================
6. VERDICT
================================================================================

F1, F2, F3, F5, F6, F7, F8, F10 are fixed and, where a plant applies, the
targeted check goes red under it (three independent CI plants, each failing at
exactly the check it attacks, exit 35). F4 is fixed in behaviour, with a dead and
wrong free path left inside the new cleanup (N2). F9 is resolved by K4-T's
wiring, which I verified in source; its plant I accepted from the author's log.

Nothing here is decorative. The one weakness that matters is N1: the TSS.rsp0
test proves the write, not the CPU's use of it. That is a coverage gap, not a
false claim, and the code is right today.

VERDICT: PASS (findings N1-N2 to the author; N5 is the known K5c flake, not this
series)
